AB  - Mycobacterium tuberculosis, the causative agent of tuberculosis (TB), primarily affects the lungs, but the infection can spread to organs such as the spine, brain and kidneys. Although TB is an airborne disease, its transmission typically requires prolonged and close contact with an infected individual. TB remains a serious global health threat, demanding unified international action for its prevention, diagnosis and treatment. This issue is addressed by Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) 3: Good Health and Well-being, particularly target 3.3, which aims to end the TB epidemic by 2030. Real-world healthcare data on TB often contains uncertainty and imprecision and fuzzy logic provides an effective framework for complex decision-making when exact information is not available. In TB research, identifying high-risk age groups is challenging because different age groups show different levels of susceptibility. To manage this uncertainty, this study integrates the VIseKriterijumska Optimizacija I Kompromisno Resenje (VIKOR) and Measuring Attractiveness by a Categorical Based Evaluation Technique (MACBETH) methods within a bipolar fuzzy framework. The bipolar approach considers both positive and negative information. MACBETH is used to build a weighted preference scale that reflects the importance of each criterion, while VIKOR identifies the best compromise solution by maximizing utility and minimizing regret. The findings show that people aged above 65 years (sub-alternatives A14, A24, and A34) were most affected between 2020 and 2022, while the 45–64 age group (A43) became more vulnerable in 2023. These changes are mainly due to the focus on coronavirus disease-19 (COVID-19), which interrupted TB treatment and monitoring services. In 2022, the alternative A3 was especially critical because the simultaneous management of TB and COVID-19 placed major pressure on healthcare systems. Furthermore, the comparative study, machine learning (ML) based validation and sensitivity analysis demonstrate that the proposed decision-making model is stable and reliable.
