AB  - As the core infrastructure of modern power grids, the safe and efficient operation of high-voltage overhead transmission lines is of paramount importance. However, traditional manual inspection suffers from numerous limitations, making it imperative to develop advanced intelligent detection algorithms that integrate the unique characteristics of inspection images to address complex task requirements. Furthermore, current research in this field lacks multi-modal fusion methods coupled with the physical field of transmission equipment, and it also faces challenges in balancing the cost of model lightweight design with feature extraction efficiency at the algorithmic design level. To address these issues, this study first constructs pseudo-thermal imaging temperature modal data based on the temperature distribution characteristics of the thermal physical field inherent in inspection images, and then designs a multi-modal attention mechanism to enhance the model's sensitivity to cross-modal information. Additionally, by integrating logical and feature distillation characteristics, this study proposes an efficient Perception Task Channel Integration Knowledge Distillation (PTCI-KD) method. Building on the Transformer architecture, two novel structural paradigms—TBFormer and Addition GLU Former are proposed for the two-level teacher-student model structure. Through the distillation process, the global modeling capability of the Transformer is transferred to the simplified addition-based paradigm of the student model, thereby addressing the shortcomings of insufficient accuracy and efficiency in multi-target inspection tasks for transmission lines under complex scenarios. Experimental results demonstrate that this method achieves State-of-the-Art (SOTA) performance on the transmission line inspection dataset while also delivering excellent performance on the transmission line connection fitting datasets and the PASCAL VOC 2007 datasets. Moreover, it effectively balances model inference efficiency and prediction accuracy, thus providing a novel solution for the comprehensive design of intelligent inspection algorithms for high-voltage transmission lines.
