AB  - The best-worst method (BWM) has been generalized under different fuzzy circumstances due to its simplicity and practicability. Since interval-valued intuitionistic fuzzy (IVIF) sets (IVIFSs) have a powerful ability to represent the uncertainty and hesitancy, extending the BWM into IVIFSs is an important research topic for group decision making (GDM) in artificial intelligence. This paper proposes a novel IVIF BWM considering multiplicative consistency. Firstly, we give multiplicative consistency for IVIF preference relations (IVIFPRs). An IVIF directed graph is introduced to design two rules for discriminating the best and worst criteria. Then, the IVIF priority weight vector (IVIFPWV) is produced through establishing a linear programming model. The consistency ratio is given to test the multiplicative consistency of IVIF reference comparisons (IVIFRCs). Aimed at unacceptably consistent IVIFRCs, an efficient technique is devised to enhance the consistency. Thus, a new IVIF BWM is proposed. Subsequently, this article develops a novel method for GDM with IVIFPRs based on the IVIF BWM. It involves the derivation of decision makers’ weights and the generation of collective IVIFPWV. The IVIF BWM has a better consistency with the increment rate of the consistency over the existing methods at least 49.79 %. The proposed GDM method has a stronger distinguishing power and needs fewer adjustments of elements.
