KW  - Instantaneous center of rotation consistency
KW  - Four wheel independent steering vehicle
KW  - Independent steering modules
KW  - Trajectory tracking
KW  - Various steering modes
AB  - Existing trajectory tracking methods fail to account for the dynamic characteristics of the high-inertia independent steering modules (ISM) in Four Wheel Independent Steering (4WIS) vehicles. This limitation makes it difficult to synchronously converge the perpendicular lines of wheel angles for various steering modes, such as same-direction, opposite-direction, front-wheel, and rear-wheel steering, onto the same desired point, significantly reducing the tracking accuracy and stability in high-speed turning scenarios. To address this, we propose an Instantaneous Center of Rotation (ICR) consistency tracking control strategy for 4WIS vehicles in high-speed turning scenarios, with two parts: ICR tracking control and ICR consistency compensation. ICR tracking control is designed with a model predictive controller based on the multi-mode error dynamics of the 4WIS vehicle and the steering dynamics model of the ISM. It converts traditional wheel-angle control into ICR control, utilizing the ICR to coordinate multi-mode steering for trajectory tracking. ICR consistency compensation is based on the randomized ensembled double Q-Learning reinforcement learning framework. It formulates the ICR non-synchronization and offset errors as reward functions, while incorporating vehicle states and tracking errors as observed states. The trained agent compensates for ICR inconsistency during trajectory tracking, enabling precise and stable tracking performance. The Hardware-in-the-Loop experimental results show that the proposed strategy can effectively enhance the trajectory tracking performance of 4WIS vehicles in high-speed cornering scenarios.
